{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat run.sh && cat sandbox/agent.sb && cat README.md && ls -la'","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\nset -u\nD=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nT=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\nR=\"$D/runs/$T-$A-r$REP\"; rm -rf \"$R\"; mkdir -p \"$R\"\nW=$(mktemp -d /tmp/h-XXXXXX); cp -R \"$D/tasks/$T/.\" \"$W/\"\nP=\"$(cat \"$D/tasks/$T.prompt\")\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$P\" > \"$R/prompt.txt\"\nTO=1200\n\ncodex_run() {\n  ( cd \"$W\" && timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n      -o \"$R/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n}\n\n# Kimi's output goes to Moonshot: its shell runs under sandbox/agent.sb with an empty scratch HOME.\nkimi_run() {\n  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n      env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n      < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n  local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n}\n\nstart=$(date +%s)\ncase $A in\n  codex) codex_run;;\n  kimi)  kimi_run;;\n  *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\nesac\nrc=$?\nend=$(date +%s)\necho \"{\\\"task\\\":\\\"$T\\\",\\\"lane\\\":\\\"$A\\\",\\\"rep\\\":$REP,\\\"exit_code\\\":$rc,\\\"wall_s\\\":$((end-start))}\" > \"$R/meta.json\"\npython3 \"$D/check_answer.py\" \"$R\" > \"$R/answer.json\"\nrm -rf \"$W\"\necho \"$T-$A-r$REP rc=$rc answer=$(python3 -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('$R/answer.json'))['final']))\" 2>/dev/null) chars\"\n;; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\ntotal 32\ndrwx------   10 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    320 Nov  9 23:00 .\ndrwxrwxrwt  647 root                 wheel  20704 Nov  9 23:00 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    384 Nov  9 23:00 .git\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     19 Nov  9 23:00 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   1174 Nov  9 23:00 README.md\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    938 Nov  9 23:00 check_answer.py\n-rwxr-xr-x    1 valentinakoniukhova  wheel   1601 Nov  9 23:00 run.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov  9 23:00 runs\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova  wheel     96 Nov  9 23:00 sandbox\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova  wheel    128 Nov  9 23:00 tasks\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
